## Modifying policies

To make changes to these policies, raise a pull request against the [aws-root-account](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/aws-root-account) repository.

Before proposing a change:

1. Identify the policy document and all of its attachments.
1. Check the target account's OU ancestry and inherited policies.
1. Assess the impact on other accounts and OUs, particularly when editing shared policies.
1. Review statement-level exceptions. Do not assume that an exception applies to the entire policy.
1. Review the Terraform plan for both policy-content and attachment changes.
1. For new restrictions or broader attachments, use a scoped pilot and agree validation and rollback steps before rollout.
1. Validate relevant operational paths, including Terraform state access, CI/CD, logging and security-service administration.
1. Check whether the policy should be included in the SCP change-alerting rule.
1. Update this runbook if policy behaviour, attachment scope or alerting coverage changes.

Update the policy inventory in `source/runbooks/modifying-scps.html.md.erb` in the `modernisation-platform` repository.

### Verifying the live policy inventory

To establish which SCPs affect a particular account:

1. In AWS Organizations, inspect the SCPs attached directly to the account.
1. Follow its parent OU chain and inspect the SCPs attached at each level, including the organisation root.
1. Include AWS-managed policies such as `FullAWSAccess`.
1. Compare live policy documents and attachments with Terraform.
1. Investigate differences, including unapplied changes, manual attachments and accounts moved between OUs.
1. Inspect the S3 organisation policy separately; it will not appear in an SCP-only inventory.

Do not treat the absence of a direct account attachment as evidence that the account has no SCP restrictions.

## Alerting

The Modernisation Platform SCP change-alerting rule is defined in:

- [`aws-root-account/management-account/terraform/alerting-modernisation-platform-scp.tf`](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/aws-root-account/blob/main/management-account/terraform/alerting-modernisation-platform-scp.tf)

The EventBridge rule runs in `us-east-1` and publishes matching AWS Organizations API events to the `modernisation-platform-scp-change-alerts` SNS topic.

It matches these operations:

- `UpdatePolicy`
- `AttachPolicy`
- `DetachPolicy`
- `DeletePolicy`

The rule explicitly filters for these policy IDs:

- Modernisation Platform Member OU SCP
- Modernisation Platform RDS Guardrails SCP
- Modernisation Platform Deny CloudTrail Delete Stop Update
- Modernisation Platform Protect Core S3 Buckets
- Modernisation Platform Protect Secure Baselines

Alerts are sent to the [#modernisation-platform-low-priority-alarms](https://mojdt.slack.com/archives/C02PFCG8M1R) Slack channel.

### Alerting limitations

The linked rule does not currently include:

- Deny AWS account root user
- Deny non-EU and non-"us-east-1" operations
- Enforce S3 KMS encryption
- Modernisation Platform S3 Block Public Access

It also does not match policy creation or account-move events. Moving an account can change its inherited restrictions without changing a policy document or attachment.

Do not rely on this rule as comprehensive monitoring of every change affecting Modernisation Platform's effective organisation policies.

